PATCH 307: register + reconstruct FUN_0000_2471 = the phase-0x1c render-script DEPTH-SORT builder
(script entry 2 @DGROUP:0x6c82).  asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=ES=DGROUP=0x1c00).

After patch 306 advanced the 22dd cursor past 0x41c7 it stalled on entry 2 = 0x2471 (another unpromoted
engine mid-entry -> fmap TRAP -> no cursor advance -> spin).  2471 walks the mission-object roster via
the c33c iterator (call near [DGROUP:0x1630], patch 292; CF via g_fist_cf, returned si via
g_fist_iter_si -- the 378e/patch-292 idiom), projects each found object (3eb3 -> e189 extender op-0x50),
computes its view distance (8e8 -> DAT_1000_c458/c45a), inserts it into a distance-sorted singly-linked
node list (DGROUP:0x4ba2..), then advances the render cursor.  Ghidra never promoted 0x2471 -> registered
in the fist_icall fmap.  Base-loss rebase: es=DS=DGROUP; every bx/di/si near-offset -> g_mem+0x1c000+off.

OBSERVED-REACHED on the genuine BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT AZER1 run: the roster is EMPTY on the first cockpit
frame (c33c returns CF on the first call, gdb-confirmed via a FIST_2471DBG probe -> zero FOUND), so the
loop exits immediately and the found body (3eb3/8e8/insertion-sort) is DORMANT.  The found body is
reconstructed faithfully from the asm for completeness; its 3eb3->e189 op-0x50 point projection is the
extender projection service (not yet wired -> imprecise, a documented residual analogous to a20d's
a192/0459), so a POPULATED roster's depth-sort is a pending refinement, not exercised on the reached path.
EFFECT: the 22dd cursor advances 41c7->2471->286e->3b59->23ce (23ce sets c450=0 -> the 22dd FRAME
COMPLETES) -> 459a proceeds into the 209e paint walk and reaches the op-0x24 poster 795c.  MISSION-PATH
ONLY (d548-gated) -> behaviour-neutral (verify.sh both = 19/19).

